            <ArticleTitle>[Experience in using helium-neon laser irradiation alone and in the combined therapy of myocardial infarct and other forms of IHD].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>13-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>349 chronic sufferers from coronary heart disease (functional class II-IV) were exposed to He-Ne laser radiation, received alpha-tocopherol acetate, solcoseryl, mildronate. Alleviation of pain syndrome, quicker increase of exercise tolerance were observed in patients treated with combined regimens: i.v. laser radiation+alpha-tocopherol acetate, i.v. laser therapy+alpha-tocopherol acetate+solcoseryl. Solcoseryl proved efficient against arrhythmia, positive trends in lipid peroxidation were observed in the use of preradiation antioxidants. It is thought valid to use drug &quot;protection&quot; in laser therapy of CHD, especially in growing intensity of the exposure and power of the beam, to control parameters of coagulation, hemostasis, microcirculation and lipid peroxidation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
